{
  "FormatVersion": 3,
  "Id": "284beba2-abf3-43d0-b8fb-8c3fc348a0be"/*SpaceMouse*/,
  "Description": "Reads the translation, rotation and buttons of a 3Dconnexion SpaceMouse.\n\nTranslation and Rotation are about -1..1 at full deflection, in TiXL's axes: X right, Y up, and pushing the cap away is -Z. The State dictionary holds the same values plus Button0 and Button1. While the SpaceMouse flies the camera (Settings → Input Devices → SpaceMouse → Use for), the outputs stay at rest.\n\nOn Linux the device is read directly, without spacenavd; the settings show whether it was found and how to grant access. In the Player it always drives operators.\n\nAKA: 3D mouse, SpaceNavigator\n\nUse in combination with [SelectFloatFromDict], [SelectBoolFromFloatDict] or the Vector3 outputs directly.",
